    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d582">

                <pb facs="0606" n="600" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg600"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Sir Julian Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-09-06"><hi rendition="#italic">September 6,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 18th ultimo, in which you state that you are
                    informed by your Government that the German Government is ready to take charge
                    of Mataafa and eleven other chiefs on the Samoan Islands and keep them in the
                    Marshall Islands, the expense of their maintenance to be divided between the
                    three powers.</p>
                <p>In view of the concurrence of Her Majesty’s Government, as expressed in your
                    note, this arrangement is assented to by the Government of the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>I should be pleased to be advised of the probable expense to be so entailed.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
